    "study_design": "Multicenter randomized, double-blind, parallel-group, 28-week study. Randomization was at a 1:1 ratio, but the method of randomization was not specified.",
    "inclusion_criteria": "Male or female in- and outpatients (ages 18–75 years) with schizophrenia (DSM-IV); baseline score of 42 or higher on the Brief Psychiatric Rating Scale; score of 4 or higher on at least one positive symptom item of the Positive and Negative Syndrome Scale; score of 4 or higher on the severity of illness scale of the Clinical Global Impression (CGI).",
    "exclusion_criteria": "Participation in a clinical trial of another drug within 1 month before study entry; treatment with an injectable depot antipsychotic within one treatment cycle before study entry; treatment with clozapine within the 7 days before enrollment; prior use of olanzapine or ziprasidone within 6 months of the study’s start and withdrawal due to clinically important and/or intolerable adverse events or lack of treatment response; congenital long QT syndrome, QTc interval longer than 500 msec, or any ECG abnormality that would confound measurement of the QT interval at visit 1 or 2; DSM-IV substance dependence within the past month; serious, unstable illness.",
    "study_setting": "12 sites in Europe and North and South America; included both inpatients and outpatients.",
    "source_of_recruitment": "12 sites in Europe and North and South America",
    "number_of_participants_randomized": "548 (277 to olanzapine, 271 to ziprasidone)",
    "number_of_participants_analyzed": "Olanzapine: 268; Ziprasidone: 261 (for primary outcome analysis)",
    "dropout_reasons": "Adverse events, aggravation of psychosis, lack of efficacy, lost to follow-up, patient decision, criteria not met, sponsor decision, physician decision.",
